Map data

  The Docker images published from this project embed databases derived from
  OpenStreetMap data: Valhalla routing tiles, a Photon geocoding index, and a
  PMTiles vector tile database.

  Map data (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the Open Database
  License (ODbL) 1.0: https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/
  OSM extracts are downloaded from Geofabrik: https://download.geofabrik.de/

  These derivative databases are themselves made available under ODbL 1.0.
  Per ODbL section 4.6, the full derivative databases are the freely pullable
  images at ghcr.io/roma8ok/getmapstack/{country}, and the method of creating
  them is the public build pipeline in build/valhalla/, build/photon/, and
  build/planetiler/ applied to the Geofabrik extracts above.

  If you publicly use routing or geocoding results from these images (for
  example in an application or on a map), you must credit OpenStreetMap:
  "(c) OpenStreetMap contributors" with a link to
  https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
  See: https://osmfoundation.org/wiki/Licence/Attribution_Guidelines

  The vector tile schema follows OpenMapTiles, available under CC-BY 4.0:
  https://openmaptiles.org/ Low-zoom context data comes from Natural Earth,
  public domain: https://www.naturalearthdata.com/ Coastline water polygons
  come from osmdata.openstreetmap.de, available under ODbL 1.0. Maps rendered
  from these tiles must show visible credit:
  "(c) OpenMapTiles (c) OpenStreetMap contributors"

Third-party software

  The published images also bundle third-party software components (Valhalla,
  prime_server, Photon, Martin, Ubuntu packages) and third-party map design
  assets: bundled Noto fonts, and the OpenFreeMap Bright style with its icons
  (https://github.com/hyperknot/openfreemap-styles, a fork of OpenMapTiles'
  OSM Bright). Their license texts ship inside each image: see
  /usr/share/doc/getmapstack/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES and
  /usr/share/doc/valhalla-deps/.

  This repository additionally carries one of those design assets outside the
  images: demo/isochrone-wave/src/styles/dark.json is a verbatim copy of the
  OpenFreeMap Dark style from the same upstream project and under the same
  terms - style code BSD 3-Clause, style design CC-BY 4.0, the fork's own
  modifications MIT. It is adapted at runtime, not edited in place. Maps drawn
  with it must carry the OpenMapTiles credit named above; the demo takes that
  credit from the tile server's own TileJSON and renders it on the map.
